## Sources & references

[^1]: The roughly 5 / 15 / 50 / 150 layering of human social networks comes from Robin Dunbar's work on social brain hypothesis and support cliques (Dunbar, *How Many Friends Does One Person Need?*, and subsequent papers). The innermost ~5 is the "support clique" associated with strongest emotional support.
[^2]: On disclosure and closeness: Aron et al. (1997), the "experimental generation of interpersonal closeness" study (the 36 questions), demonstrates escalating mutual self-disclosure rapidly deepens perceived closeness.
